  "body": "## What happens\n\nAt a section end, the Mazak post writes `M9` and `M5`. It lifts Z only when the operation asks for \"Go home\". The default after-action is \"Continue\", which writes no PARAM. The next section then writes `G17 G90 G54 G40 G49 G80`, then `T<n> M6` and `G43 H<n>`.\n\nThus the control reads `G49` while the tool is at the clearance height of the previous operation. The Mazak EIA/ISO programming manual says that `G49` moves the axis to remove the length offset. Z can then move down by the tool length, into or near the part.\n\nThe text of the `safeRetract` option says \"Z retract command before tool changes and at program end\". The post writes it only at program end and on \"Go home\".\n\n## Expected\n\nBefore each tool change after the first, the post retracts Z with the `safeRetract` method (`G91 G28 Z0` then `G90`, or `G53 G00 Z<safeRetractZ>`). Then it writes `G49` and `T M6`.\n\n## Evidence (upstream main `eafe6aec6`)\n\n- `assets/posts/mazak.cps:648-671`: `endPreamble` writes no Z retract.\n- `assets/posts/mazak.cps:591`: the preamble writes `G49`.\n- `assets/posts/mazak.cps:597-598`: the preamble writes `T M6` and `G43 H`.\n- `assets/posts/mazak.cps:48-58`: the `safeRetract` option text.\n- `assets/posts/mazak.cps:226-240`: `retractHome`. Only `afterOp` (`:633`, `:640`) and the program end call it.\n- `crates/post/src/post/after_op.rs:22-25`, `:56-58`: the default \"Continue\" writes no PARAM, and the engine adds no retract.\n- `assets/posts/fanuc.cps:811-818` and `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps:868-875`: the same preamble order (`G49`, then `T M6`) with no retract before it.\n\nFound by the post audit against the Mazak manuals (#4130).\n\n## Done means\n\n- A two-tool Mazak program writes a Z retract before the second `G49` and `T M6`. A golden pins it.\n- `fanuc.cps` and `doosan-dnm.cps` get the same check. Each post is fixed or recorded as not affected, with the reason.\n",
